1
00:01:37,239 --> 00:01:38,840
How did the surveillance notice get lost?

2
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:41,200
Maybe the nanny threw it out by mistake.

3
00:01:41,959 --> 00:01:43,040
Good thing Lawyer Ding found it.

4
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,280
Do you know that without the notice,

5
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:46,359
how hard it is to find someone?

6
00:01:47,519 --> 00:01:48,280
Thank you.

7
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:53,439
Here, leave your thumbprint.

8
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:54,560
Excuse me.

9
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,000
Where is the restroom?

10
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:56,959
Over there.

11
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:57,920
Thank you.

12
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:16,520
Just find one thing at my place,

13
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:17,800
and I'm sure

14
00:02:18,319 --> 00:02:20,680
you'll find the Sham Litigation Base.

15
00:02:22,919 --> 00:02:23,759
Why?

16
00:02:24,919 --> 00:02:26,919
Turn it over to the Economic Crime Investigation Division,

17
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,319
or Prosecutor's Office. Isn't it faster?

18
00:02:30,919 --> 00:02:32,199
That key

19
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,879
is a spare key to Zhao Yijie's office.

20
00:02:35,199 --> 00:02:36,240
If the police go

21
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,439
and don't find anything,

22
00:02:37,639 --> 00:02:39,199
it'll only tip him off.

23
00:02:40,719 --> 00:02:43,599
So someone from Rujie should sneak in.

24
00:02:45,759 --> 00:02:47,560
Does Zhao Yijie know you have his key?

25
00:02:48,039 --> 00:02:49,159
Of course not.

26
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:50,639
I secretly made a copy.

27
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,280
So you want me to sneak in

28
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:56,280
and find clues to this base's location.

29
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:11,639
The key is to find a car key.

30
00:03:12,759 --> 00:03:13,800
That key of his

31
00:03:14,039 --> 00:03:15,919
is hidden in a picture frame in his office.

32
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,800
For places he fears being followed to,

33
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,000
he uses a spare car.

34
00:03:27,199 --> 00:03:28,319
And that spare vehicle

35
00:03:28,439 --> 00:03:30,000
is in the law firm's underground garage.

36
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,560
You can look up its frequent addresses.

37
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,560
And once you find the car,

38
00:03:38,919 --> 00:03:40,800
whether you check its driving routes

39
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,240
or track its license plate,

40
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,000
you won't be far from finding the base.

41
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,360
Lao Yu.

42
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:02,960
Ding Ning, I'm right here.

43
00:04:05,639 --> 00:04:06,599
I was just looking for you.

44
00:04:07,159 --> 00:04:08,840
I'll buy some paintbrushes for Awu first.

45
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:09,759
He's been asking for them for days.

46
00:04:09,759 --> 00:04:10,840
We'll meet over there later.

47
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:12,240
I bought you breakfast.

48
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:13,560
Come over and have a bite. Come on.

49
00:04:14,319 --> 00:04:15,280
You bought so much.

50
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,480
I noticed every day when you leave,

51
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,839
you just get an iced coffee,

52
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,839
and just a piece of bread.

53
00:04:21,839 --> 00:04:24,000
You know how important breakfast is.

54
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:24,800
Come on, come on.

55
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:26,279
I didn't know what you'd like,

56
00:04:26,279 --> 00:04:27,759
so I bought a bit of everything.

57
00:04:27,759 --> 00:04:28,360
Come on.

58
00:04:30,079 --> 00:04:31,279
Aren't you going to wake Awu up?

59
00:04:32,439 --> 00:04:34,480
Kids need more sleep to grow tall.

60
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:38,519
Do you want some porridge?

61
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:39,759
I'll pass. You have it.

62
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:41,079
I'll have it then.

63
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:45,120
Here. Take your time eating.

64
00:04:52,439 --> 00:04:54,360
Alright, I'll take my time eating.

65
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,160
You take your time talking.

66
00:04:56,959 --> 00:04:57,600
Go ahead.

67
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,800
You know I got mad at you before.

68
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:05,759
It was about you joining Rujie.

69
00:05:05,759 --> 00:05:07,839
I've been thinking about it since.

70
00:05:10,079 --> 00:05:11,079
Have you ever thought about

71
00:05:11,879 --> 00:05:13,399
opening your own law firm?

72
00:05:17,759 --> 00:05:18,800
Your own law firm.

73
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:22,439
We could start an independent firm together.

74
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:23,519
Think about it.

75
00:05:23,639 --> 00:05:25,040
Having your own law firm,

76
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,920
you could safely and freely

77
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,399
do what you want to do.

78
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:29,680
Plus,

79
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,040
with me around, you won't lack cases.

80
00:05:34,279 --> 00:05:36,319
We'd have to plan that carefully.

81
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:39,519
I need to finish my current cases first.

82
00:05:40,639 --> 00:05:42,319
Take Mrs. Lin's case, for example.

83
00:05:42,319 --> 00:05:43,399
That one is easy enough.

84
00:05:43,759 --> 00:05:45,560
But Liang Zidong's case is very complex.

85
00:05:46,959 --> 00:05:49,000
I'm not asking you to quit immediately.

86
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:49,720
At least wait for me

87
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:52,399
until my three-year non-compete is up.

88
00:05:53,399 --> 00:05:55,720
Do you remember my mentee, Ma Tingting?

89
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,480
The one at the Prosecutor's Office.

90
00:05:58,160 --> 00:05:59,720
We had a get-together not long ago.

91
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,839
She told me she was exhausted.

92
00:06:01,839 --> 00:06:03,480
I heard she's in a task force

93
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:06,959
responsible for investigating Fuxia Group.

94
00:06:09,199 --> 00:06:10,319
Do you know what I mean?

95
00:06:12,879 --> 00:06:14,319
In Liang Zidong's case,

96
00:06:15,439 --> 00:06:17,199
they must be investigating Zhao Yijie too.

97
00:06:17,519 --> 00:06:19,879
And his protective umbrella.

98
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
That's why I'm telling you,

99
00:06:22,519 --> 00:06:25,199
Rujie really isn't as simple as you think.

100
00:06:25,839 --> 00:06:27,000
Didn't you say it yourself?

101
00:06:27,319 --> 00:06:30,319
Liang Zidong said they have a

102
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,279
Sham Litigation Base, right?

103
00:06:32,439 --> 00:06:34,079
Isn't that place just

104
00:06:34,079 --> 00:06:36,279
a headquarters for criminal activities?

105
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:40,120
Haven't you thought about reporting it?

106
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:46,439
I have.

107
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,399
Of course I have.

108
00:06:48,839 --> 00:06:51,240
But I fear it'll be like when I reported you.

109
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:53,399
I might regret it afterward.

110
00:06:54,519 --> 00:06:56,040
Doing the right thing

111
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,639
at least leaves no regrets.

112
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:00,759
Look, our relationship

113
00:07:00,879 --> 00:07:02,319
is pretty good now, isn't it?

114
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:04,959
I think

115
00:07:04,959 --> 00:07:05,720
after you report it,

116
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:08,319
you can justifiably quit.

117
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:10,560
And make a much cleaner exit.

118
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:11,920
Right?

119
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:15,560
It's just a suggestion,

120
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:17,480
giving you another option.

121
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:20,480
You decide what to do yourself.

122
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:24,519
Are you going to the prison later?

123
00:07:25,759 --> 00:07:27,000
Are you just going to wear that?

124
00:07:37,959 --> 00:07:39,000
Fiancée.

125
00:07:41,879 --> 00:07:42,720
And him?

126
00:07:43,399 --> 00:07:44,959
Son. Adopted.

127
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,120
Is he their child?

128
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,439
No, he's adopted.

129
00:07:47,439 --> 00:07:49,759
It says "adopted" here.

130
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:52,160
Our rules here state that

131
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:53,480
only family members can go in.

132
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:54,480
Understood.

133
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,279
They can go in. I won't.

134
00:07:57,439 --> 00:07:58,600
Alright, you two can go in.

135
00:07:58,600 --> 00:07:59,920
Okay. Thank you.

136
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:17,680
Awu!

137
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:19,879
Dad!

138
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,199
Dad misses you.

139
00:08:22,879 --> 00:08:24,399
How could you come here?

140
00:08:25,319 --> 00:08:26,360
You shouldn't have come.

141
00:08:26,519 --> 00:08:27,920
You can't be here.

142
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:29,560
Why did you come here?

143
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:32,200
They said I can visit you every month now.

144
00:08:34,159 --> 00:08:35,879
What? What did you say?

145
00:08:36,559 --> 00:08:38,080
Awu, stop crying.

146
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,200
Let's not waste time.

147
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,200
Didn't you have a gift for Dad?

148
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:46,720
Show it to him.

149
00:08:49,799 --> 00:08:51,000
They taught me how to write.

150
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:55,080
Look, I wrote this.

151
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:08,639
They said I wrote it wrong.

152
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:10,720
But I think

153
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:12,559
the wrong ones look better than the right.

154
00:09:12,919 --> 00:09:14,120
Okay, okay.

155
00:09:18,759 --> 00:09:22,159
Awu, did they hit you?

156
00:09:22,919 --> 00:09:23,840
They didn't hit me.

157
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:26,320
Zhao Yijie told me to go to school.

158
00:09:26,799 --> 00:09:28,000
But I don't want to go to school.

159
00:09:28,519 --> 00:09:29,840
They're all very nice.

160
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,360
But I don't like it here.

161
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:40,159
The trees here are all trimmed the same.

162
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:44,080
Everyone on the street has the same face.

163
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:46,240
The animals in the zoo

164
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:48,320
have the same faces as the people.

165
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:51,159
It's the same everywhere.

166
00:10:09,519 --> 00:10:12,200
Awu, could you ask Dad

167
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:14,320
how he got that injury?

168
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:19,360
How did you get injured?

169
00:10:25,159 --> 00:10:26,120
Dad is fine.

170
00:10:26,759 --> 00:10:29,360
Just got into a fight with a cellmate.

171
00:10:30,039 --> 00:10:31,759
It's nothing. It's nothing.

172
00:10:32,039 --> 00:10:34,480
He got it fighting someone in his cell.

173
00:10:36,159 --> 00:10:37,240
A few months ago,

174
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:38,519
a male lawyer came to see Dad.

175
00:10:38,519 --> 00:10:39,759
Dad told him about it.

176
00:10:39,759 --> 00:10:42,200
Dad is fine. Really.

177
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,240
He also said that a few months ago,

178
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,519
he mentioned it to a male lawyer

179
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:47,279
during a meeting at the detention center.

180
00:10:47,279 --> 00:10:48,240
A male lawyer?

181
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,519
Zhou Hao.

182
00:10:52,759 --> 00:10:54,399
Was that male lawyer named Zhou Hao?

183
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:55,679
Zhou Hao.

184
00:11:06,039 --> 00:11:07,000
Zhou Hao.

185
00:11:08,519 --> 00:11:09,480
Zhou Hao, you lied to me.

186
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:10,879
Those two days you went missing,

187
00:11:10,879 --> 00:11:12,480
you saw Lao Kang at the detention center, right?

188
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:14,600
Aren't you handling Mr. Liang's case?

189
00:11:15,799 --> 00:11:17,559
No wonder you've been acting so weird.

190
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,240
And after Lao Kang's case,

191
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,519
you stopped doing criminal law

192
00:11:20,519 --> 00:11:22,399
and switched to civil law under Xu Ruqing.

193
00:11:22,399 --> 00:11:23,320
Until Liang Zidong's case.

194
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,399
We'll talk about this later.

195
00:11:25,279 --> 00:11:25,879
How could...

196
00:11:25,879 --> 00:11:26,720
Mrs. Lin.

197
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:28,799
Over here.

198
00:11:29,159 --> 00:11:30,159
Lawyer Ding!

199
00:11:30,559 --> 00:11:31,320
Lawyer Ding!

200
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:32,159
Go on, go on.

201
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,759
You haven't gotten off work yet?

202
00:11:34,679 --> 00:11:36,080
Zhou Hao, I'm not done talking!

203
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:36,720
Lawyer Ding.

204
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:39,039
Mrs. Lin, I just came back for some files.

205
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:40,279
My car is still waiting downstairs.

206
00:11:40,279 --> 00:11:41,320
I have to leave right away.

207
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:42,279
That's all right.

208
00:11:42,279 --> 00:11:44,559
I just came to express my gratitude.

209
00:11:44,559 --> 00:11:47,000
You said you'd give your all to our case.

210
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,759
I thought you were just saying that.

211
00:11:48,799 --> 00:11:51,279
I didn't think you'd get us a court date.

212
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,720
And your defense statement...

213
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,200
It was written perfectly.

214
00:11:54,399 --> 00:11:55,759
I've saved it

215
00:11:55,759 --> 00:11:56,879
to make our kid

216
00:11:56,919 --> 00:11:58,720
recite it word for word.

217
00:11:58,759 --> 00:11:59,720
To let them know

218
00:11:59,879 --> 00:12:01,440
what makes a good essay.

219
00:12:01,679 --> 00:12:02,440
Thank you!

220
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:03,200
It's my job.

221
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:04,240
Oh, right.

222
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:06,279
About the job you helped Lao Lin find,

223
00:12:06,279 --> 00:12:07,519
we've sent you his resume.

224
00:12:07,519 --> 00:12:08,720
Does it look okay?

225
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:09,759
Resume?

226
00:12:09,799 --> 00:12:10,519
What resume?

227
00:12:10,519 --> 00:12:11,679
The assistant lawyer...

228
00:12:11,679 --> 00:12:13,080
named Zhao... something Jie.

229
00:12:13,279 --> 00:12:13,960
Zhao Yijie.

230
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,440
Right, he told us to send it.

231
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:15,919
He said

232
00:12:15,919 --> 00:12:18,120
you were helping Lao Lin find a new job,

233
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,799
so we hurried and prepared a resume.

234
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:24,960
I know

235
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:26,840
it's not part of your job as a lawyer.

236
00:12:26,919 --> 00:12:27,720
But

237
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:30,080
you really treat us both as friends

238
00:12:30,159 --> 00:12:31,720
to help us out this much.

239
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,480
Thank you!

240
00:12:33,679 --> 00:12:34,240
Oh, right.

241
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,679
He told us to contact this person

242
00:12:35,679 --> 00:12:36,960
to arrange an interview.

243
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:38,159
When is the interview?

244
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:40,320
Kong Dongshun.

245
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:41,000
Yes.

246
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,360
Let me go check for you.

247
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,759
Please take a seat for a moment.

248
00:12:44,919 --> 00:12:45,519
Okay.

249
00:12:47,279 --> 00:12:48,480
Kong Dongshun.

250
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:57,159
Is Kong Dongshun a lawyer at our firm?

251
00:12:57,720 --> 00:12:58,759
I've never heard of this person.

252
00:12:58,960 --> 00:12:59,799
Admin?

253
00:12:59,799 --> 00:13:01,440
A driver or an assistant, perhaps?

254
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:02,200
Look it up.

255
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,919
Why are these all Fuxia civil cases?

256
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:29,759
Assigned by Director Xu.

257
00:13:30,399 --> 00:13:31,600
Assigned by Xu Ruqing?

258
00:13:33,399 --> 00:13:35,120
Then why are the signatories all interns?

259
00:13:35,679 --> 00:13:36,600
You noticed too.

260
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:39,000
A couple of days ago, a few interns and I

261
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,200
were wondering about this too.

262
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:44,080
They let the interns do most of the work.

263
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,639
It's a chance to make some extra cash.

264
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:48,679
They were all thrilled.

265
00:13:51,159 --> 00:13:52,000
Were you doing this

266
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:54,200
before I found Liang Zidong

267
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:55,360
or after?

268
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:56,879
I've been doing it all along.

269
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:58,559
I got here before you did, right?

270
00:13:59,039 --> 00:13:59,960
I've been doing it since I arrived.

271
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,320
But after you found Mr. Liang,

272
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:04,639
these minor cases involving

273
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:06,679
mortgages, guarantees, and loans

274
00:14:06,879 --> 00:14:08,080
did start to pile up again.

275
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:10,120
Zhou Hao.

276
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:13,720
Try not to do these anymore.

277
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:15,120
If possible,

278
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:17,000
help the interns back out too.

279
00:14:20,399 --> 00:14:21,759
Does this have to do with Liang Zidong?

280
00:14:21,879 --> 00:14:23,240
I can't be sure right now.

281
00:14:23,679 --> 00:14:25,480
But if it's really what I think it is,

282
00:14:25,919 --> 00:14:27,120
the interns are too inexperienced

283
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:27,759
to tell

284
00:14:27,759 --> 00:14:29,000
if it involves sham litigation

285
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:29,879
or forged evidence.

286
00:14:30,519 --> 00:14:31,600
If they really start arresting people,

287
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:32,879
will they arrest Xu Ruqing?

288
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:35,279
They'll arrest those of you who signed.

289
00:14:36,759 --> 00:14:38,039
Sham litigation?

290
00:14:39,159 --> 00:14:40,080
That can't be, right?

291
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:44,000
Many of these cases were filed long ago.

292
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,039
If there really was a problem,

293
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:54,600
the firm's reputation would be ruined.

294
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:57,039
Who'd dare hire Rujie after that?

295
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,600
Did you find Kong Dongshun?

296
00:15:03,759 --> 00:15:04,480
No.

297
00:15:04,879 --> 00:15:06,679
I even checked the list of employees

298
00:15:06,679 --> 00:15:07,480
who left in the past few years,

299
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:09,159
and there's no such person at all.

300
00:15:11,519 --> 00:15:12,320
What's up with him?

301
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:16,039
I held a concert for a friend's daughter.

302
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:17,120
Let's go watch it together.

303
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:22,279
It's nothing.

304
00:15:22,799 --> 00:15:24,080
Please keep an eye on Mrs. Lin for me.

305
00:15:34,039 --> 00:15:35,399
I'm warning you one more time.

306
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:37,799
Any cases related to Fuxia Group,

307
00:15:37,799 --> 00:15:38,720
stop working on them.

308
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:40,320
You must back out of this, got it?

309
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:41,360
I'm not joking with you.

310
00:16:02,759 --> 00:16:03,519
Have you eaten?

311
00:16:04,759 --> 00:16:05,559
Want some?

312
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:18,919
What's wrong?

313
00:16:19,679 --> 00:16:20,919
I think you're quite conflicted.

314
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,879
What are you talking about?

315
00:16:25,519 --> 00:16:27,240
You came all the way to my house...

316
00:16:27,519 --> 00:16:28,879
just to have a heart-to-heart with me?

317
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,759
I do want to have a heart-to-heart.

318
00:16:32,639 --> 00:16:33,519
Then forget it.

319
00:16:34,159 --> 00:16:35,960
For a heart-to-heart, go find Lao Yu.

320
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,759
About the Sham Litigation Base...

321
00:16:42,159 --> 00:16:42,960
I know about it.

322
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,279
Liang Zidong told you this?

323
00:17:01,919 --> 00:17:02,440
Yes.

324
00:17:03,919 --> 00:17:05,240
Not only did he tell me,

325
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:07,559
he also asked me to report it,

326
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:13,559
just like I reported Yu Songfan back then.

327
00:17:30,839 --> 00:17:33,160
They say you're a master manipulator.

328
00:17:36,079 --> 00:17:37,039
But you blew it.

329
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:39,759
You helped Mrs. Lin's family, who are strangers,

330
00:17:39,759 --> 00:17:40,640
find jobs,

331
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:43,119
and solved their problems from the root.

332
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:45,440
You held a concert for Kong Dongshun's daughter,

333
00:17:45,839 --> 00:17:47,599
fulfilling a father's wish.

334
00:17:48,759 --> 00:17:49,599
I guess

335
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:52,720
you running the Sham Litigation Base

336
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:56,319
is to save thousands of jobs at Fuxia Group.

337
00:17:57,839 --> 00:17:58,559
Right?

338
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:05,319
You clearly have things you value deeply.

339
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:08,079
I know you care about me and Yu Songfan.

340
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:09,880
You have many people you care about.

341
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:11,759
But on one hand, you care about us,

342
00:18:11,759 --> 00:18:13,200
and on the other, you're using us.

343
00:18:14,799 --> 00:18:16,000
Aren't you tired of living like this?

344
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:18,720
I'm really not sure anymore.

345
00:18:19,079 --> 00:18:21,400
I fear it'll be like reporting Yu Songfan.

346
00:18:21,799 --> 00:18:22,599
Because doing something

347
00:18:22,599 --> 00:18:23,720
I thought was right,

348
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:25,440
ended up hurting innocent people.

349
00:18:25,799 --> 00:18:27,319
I'm also afraid of dragging Rujie down.

350
00:18:27,319 --> 00:18:28,160
Dragging Zhou Hao down.

351
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,640
Dragging down the interns at the firm.

352
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:32,759
And dragging you down too.

353
00:18:37,359 --> 00:18:38,079
Drag me down?

354
00:18:40,559 --> 00:18:41,880
Are you really that confident now?

355
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:47,599
How could you drag me down?

356
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:53,799
Liang Zidong, Yu Songfan,

357
00:18:53,839 --> 00:18:54,880
even Xu Ruqing,

358
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:57,200
not a single person is on your side.

359
00:18:58,200 --> 00:19:00,559
Everyone wants me to report you.

360
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:02,839
The more it's like this,

361
00:19:02,839 --> 00:19:04,400
the more I feel things aren't that simple.

362
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:06,400
I know even if I ask you

363
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:07,680
what's really hidden behind all this,

364
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,920
you won't tell me.

365
00:19:09,079 --> 00:19:10,039
But at least,

366
00:19:11,519 --> 00:19:14,000
I hope you can stop the sham litigations.

367
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:15,480
At least walk away from it.

368
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:17,440
For you,

369
00:19:19,039 --> 00:19:20,519
it might be the best choice.

370
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:24,240
Stop exhausting yourself, okay?

371
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:27,319
The Sham Litigation Base cannot stop.

372
00:19:38,519 --> 00:19:39,200
Why?

373
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,279
Why can't you stop?

374
00:19:43,079 --> 00:19:44,240
Since it's come to this,

375
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:45,319
I'll be honest.

376
00:19:46,319 --> 00:19:47,000
Ding Ning.

377
00:19:48,079 --> 00:19:49,279
Help me just this once, okay?

378
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:50,440
Don't report it.

379
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:52,920
Don't you get it?

380
00:19:56,240 --> 00:19:57,200
Even though I don't know

381
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,480
why everyone wants me

382
00:19:58,480 --> 00:19:59,400
to report it,

383
00:19:59,839 --> 00:20:00,599
if you don't want

384
00:20:00,599 --> 00:20:02,799
you and everyone at Rujie to be implicated,

385
00:20:03,799 --> 00:20:05,599
disband the Sham Litigation Base

386
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:07,759
and leave Fuxia Group alone.

387
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:09,920
But my guess is, this Sham Litigation Base

388
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:10,920
will act like a bomb,

389
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:12,839
blowing your targets to pieces.

390
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,680
And just like Liang Zidong said,

391
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:15,839
your backers

392
00:20:16,319 --> 00:20:17,960
will be able to hide even deeper.

393
00:20:18,599 --> 00:20:19,359
As for you,

394
00:20:20,519 --> 00:20:23,119
you've become a discarded pawn.

395
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:36,000
This kid is pretty hard to find.

396
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:36,960
Yeah.

397
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:39,920
Here.

398
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:40,599
Right here.

399
00:21:06,039 --> 00:21:06,759
Lao Fan

400
00:21:17,039 --> 00:21:18,559
Has anyone seen the kid from this family?

401
00:21:18,559 --> 00:21:20,119
Haven't seen him. No idea.

402
00:21:20,359 --> 00:21:21,960
His family works at the construction site.

403
00:21:23,039 --> 00:21:23,720
Let's go.

404
00:21:23,839 --> 00:21:24,640
Thank you.

405
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:34,359
Hello.

406
00:21:35,119 --> 00:21:36,440
Excuse me, which one is Lu Zhiyong?

407
00:21:37,039 --> 00:21:37,759
Over there.

408
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:38,839
The shortest one.

409
00:21:39,039 --> 00:21:39,880
Thanks.

410
00:21:40,079 --> 00:21:40,839
Lu Zhiyong!

411
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:43,119
Lu Zhiyong!

412
00:21:45,160 --> 00:21:45,960
Stop right there!

413
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:47,079
Don't run! Stop!

414
00:21:47,079 --> 00:21:47,880
Don't you run!

415
00:21:48,119 --> 00:21:48,960
It wasn't a big deal to begin with.

416
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:50,319
But running makes it worse.

417
00:21:50,519 --> 00:21:51,920
Stop! Stop! Stop!

418
00:21:53,119 --> 00:21:53,759
Get up.

419
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:55,160
Is your name Lu Zhiyong?

420
00:21:55,279 --> 00:21:56,079
What about it?

421
00:21:56,119 --> 00:21:56,920
You'd better behave.

422
00:21:57,519 --> 00:21:59,079
Or you and your mom will lose your jobs.

423
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:01,880
I'm talking to him.

424
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:04,640
We already know all about you.

425
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:07,000
Your dad fell and was paralyzed at the site.

426
00:22:07,079 --> 00:22:08,240
The site didn't pay you any compensation,

427
00:22:08,359 --> 00:22:10,000
but let you and your mom do odd jobs.

428
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:10,599
Right?

429
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:12,440
I didn't do anything wrong.

430
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:14,039
But you lied about your age to work.

431
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:15,880
Come back to the station with me first.

432
00:22:16,119 --> 00:22:17,240
We'll hold your boss accountable later.

433
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:18,359
Take him away.

434
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:19,440
Let's go. Move.

435
00:22:20,160 --> 00:22:21,079
Your hand is scraped.

436
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:22,000
Is it serious?

437
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:26,400
Can we contact your mom?

438
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:29,839
The site didn't give you compensation,

439
00:22:29,839 --> 00:22:30,960
so you went and stole people's money?

440
00:22:31,759 --> 00:22:32,599
I didn't steal.

441
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:34,559
What about your friend who was with you?

442
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:35,920
He didn't steal either.

443
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:38,079
Why pick a lock into someone's house?

444
00:22:38,759 --> 00:22:39,480
Just to take a look.

445
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:40,519
Look at what?

446
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:44,079
At how the house my dad built looks now.

447
00:22:44,079 --> 00:22:45,200
Your dad built it?

448
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:47,079
Wasn't your dad working at the site

449
00:22:47,079 --> 00:22:48,519
when he fell and got paralyzed?

450
00:22:48,519 --> 00:22:49,559
How could he have built it?

451
00:22:49,559 --> 00:22:51,920
He built lots of buildings before he fell.

452
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:53,440
Then why did you

453
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:54,799
push a paralyzed old man

454
00:22:54,799 --> 00:22:56,519
from his home to the police station?

455
00:22:56,839 --> 00:22:57,799
To take him out for some fun.

456
00:22:58,400 --> 00:22:59,799
Why don't you take your dad out?

457
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,400
Why take out an old man you don't know?

458
00:23:02,119 --> 00:23:02,920
He has a wheelchair.

459
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:04,720
My dad doesn't.

460
00:23:09,799 --> 00:23:10,440
Do you know

461
00:23:10,440 --> 00:23:12,000
that picking a lock is illegal?

462
00:23:14,880 --> 00:23:15,839
Even if you didn't know that,

463
00:23:16,279 --> 00:23:18,279
you should know you'd get caught stealing.

464
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:19,559
I didn't steal anything.

465
00:23:19,799 --> 00:23:20,839
You're still lying.

466
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:22,359
The security cameras recorded it all.

467
00:23:22,759 --> 00:23:24,559
And what about your shorter little friend?

468
00:23:24,799 --> 00:23:26,000
What's your friend's name?

469
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:30,519
Did you give the money you stole

470
00:23:30,759 --> 00:23:31,920
to your mom already?

471
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,400
I didn't steal.

472
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:35,039
I just went to play.

473
00:23:38,559 --> 00:23:39,720
We found the surveillance footage.

474
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:40,880
Good.

475
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:42,720
Think about it carefully.

476
00:23:43,079 --> 00:23:44,319
Contact the community workers.

477
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:47,640
Four households reported the crime.

478
00:23:47,640 --> 00:23:49,240
Two of them had security cameras.

479
00:23:49,240 --> 00:23:51,240
The footage shows Lu Zhiyong

480
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:52,240
just walking around looking.

481
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:53,200
Right before leaving, he even

482
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:54,160
cleaned up the place a bit.

483
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:56,960
So he's acting like a cleaning fairy?

484
00:23:58,519 --> 00:23:59,400
What about the other one?

485
00:23:59,799 --> 00:24:00,519
The other one.

486
00:24:00,519 --> 00:24:02,160
Only this one captured both kids.

487
00:24:02,359 --> 00:24:04,519
But because of the angle

488
00:24:04,759 --> 00:24:06,119
and the fact the other kid is too short,

489
00:24:06,119 --> 00:24:07,119
we couldn't get a shot of their face.

490
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:08,279
We can only rely on you to ask him.

491
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:09,440
Is there any more?

492
00:24:10,079 --> 00:24:12,279
The rest of the footage is from hallways.

493
00:24:12,279 --> 00:24:13,839
It only proves they picked locks to enter.

494
00:24:13,839 --> 00:24:14,960
There's no way to directly prove

495
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:16,079
that they committed theft.

496
00:24:17,079 --> 00:24:19,359
I remember at the paralyzed man's house,

497
00:24:19,359 --> 00:24:20,960
his daughter said she lost 2,000 yuan.

498
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:23,880
Xiao Li's forensics team went to check,

499
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:25,319
and there were no signs of a break-in.

500
00:24:25,519 --> 00:24:26,279
When they asked again,

501
00:24:26,279 --> 00:24:27,839
the old man's kids finally told the truth.

502
00:24:27,839 --> 00:24:29,000
They didn't lose any money at all.

503
00:24:29,160 --> 00:24:30,119
They didn't lose any money?

504
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:33,119
So they were trying to extort the kid?

505
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:34,039
Exactly.

506
00:24:34,039 --> 00:24:36,440
So a theft charge probably won't stick.

507
00:24:36,799 --> 00:24:39,640
Then should we proceed with trespassing

508
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:40,640
and send it to the Prosecutor's Office?

509
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:41,440
Let's wait.

510
00:24:42,039 --> 00:24:43,559
First, let's contact the kid's parents

511
00:24:43,839 --> 00:24:45,279
and find the other kid before we decide.

512
00:24:45,759 --> 00:24:46,559
Got it.

513
00:24:49,839 --> 00:24:51,599
It's not that I forgot.

514
00:24:51,599 --> 00:24:54,200
But since I was house-hunting all day

515
00:24:56,319 --> 00:24:58,000
and I had to pick up my kid from school,

516
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:59,160
I couldn't make it.

517
00:24:59,559 --> 00:25:01,400
Right, I'll meet you tomorrow.

518
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:02,319
Sorry about that.

519
00:25:03,519 --> 00:25:04,279
Okay.

520
00:25:05,480 --> 00:25:07,359
Take out your homework.

521
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:08,960
Do your homework first.

522
00:25:09,559 --> 00:25:11,200
And then Grandpa will go cook dinner.

523
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:12,160
I don't want to do my homework.

524
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,559
I want to watch TV.

525
00:25:13,839 --> 00:25:15,319
How can you do that?

526
00:25:15,359 --> 00:25:17,279
Finish your homework before watching TV.

527
00:25:17,279 --> 00:25:18,119
Be a good boy.

528
00:25:20,640 --> 00:25:21,440
What's wrong?

529
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:22,920
Why are you throwing a tantrum?

530
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:25,559
Grandpa will do your homework with you.

531
00:25:25,559 --> 00:25:26,440
It'll be fast.

532
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:28,880
Right? Grandpa will teach you how.

533
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:30,400
Come here. Be good.

534
00:25:36,680 --> 00:25:38,240
Do adults have to do homework too?

535
00:25:39,279 --> 00:25:40,079
Of course.

536
00:25:40,599 --> 00:25:41,920
Then I'd rather not grow up.

537
00:25:41,920 --> 00:25:43,559
My teacher was lying after all.

538
00:25:43,559 --> 00:25:44,400
Why?

539
00:25:44,599 --> 00:25:46,119
Today, my teacher said

540
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:47,920
things get easier when you grow up.

541
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:49,480
You don't need a backpack anymore.

542
00:25:51,559 --> 00:25:53,559
My classmates all want to grow up.

543
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:55,119
Some of my classmates

544
00:25:56,359 --> 00:25:57,519
want to be scientists.

545
00:25:58,079 --> 00:25:59,240
Some classmates

546
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,039
want to be athletes.

547
00:26:01,759 --> 00:26:03,440
Some want to be doctors.

548
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:04,920
They asked me,

549
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:06,519
"What do you want to be?"

550
00:26:06,640 --> 00:26:07,960
How did you answer?

551
00:26:08,759 --> 00:26:09,839
I said I didn't know.

552
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:11,640
I definitely don't want to do

553
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:13,920
the work Zhao Yijie and Ding Ning do.

554
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:15,920
Because they never come home.

555
00:26:17,599 --> 00:26:20,160
I don't want a job where I can't go home.

556
00:26:20,160 --> 00:26:21,160
Grandpa is the best.

557
00:26:21,279 --> 00:26:22,359
You're home every day.

558
00:26:24,359 --> 00:26:26,599
Grandpa, did you use to work?

559
00:26:27,039 --> 00:26:28,599
What kind of work did you do?

560
00:26:45,720 --> 00:26:47,599
Be good. Grandpa needs to make a call.

561
00:26:48,920 --> 00:26:50,039
Do your homework.

562
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:53,319
Hello, Lao Wang.

563
00:26:53,559 --> 00:26:54,440
Lao Yu.

564
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:56,400
Lao Yu.

565
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:58,759
Are the results of my medical checkup out?

566
00:26:58,920 --> 00:26:59,720
Not yet.

567
00:27:01,640 --> 00:27:02,880
The results really aren't out.

568
00:27:03,759 --> 00:27:05,559
Your situation is a bit complicated.

569
00:27:05,559 --> 00:27:06,599
Okay, just tell me.

570
00:27:06,599 --> 00:27:08,319
How much time do I have left?

571
00:27:08,720 --> 00:27:09,440
Lao Yu.

572
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:11,240
Don't add any more

573
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:12,920
unnecessary stress on yourself.

574
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:13,359
Think about it.

575
00:27:13,359 --> 00:27:14,440
You've spent your life

576
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:15,640
standing for fairness and justice,

577
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:17,200
upright and honest.

578
00:27:17,559 --> 00:27:19,359
Honestly, you've had a good run.

579
00:27:20,160 --> 00:27:21,519
Just enjoy your retirement.

580
00:27:21,519 --> 00:27:22,400
That's better than anything.

581
00:27:23,519 --> 00:27:25,160
Once I have a definitive result,

582
00:27:25,640 --> 00:27:27,039
I'll let you know immediately, okay?

583
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:50,839
Awu!

584
00:27:53,079 --> 00:27:53,880
Awu!

585
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:04,440
Grandpa!

586
00:28:06,960 --> 00:28:08,119
Wake up, Grandpa!

587
00:28:09,599 --> 00:28:10,319
Grandpa!

588
00:28:11,759 --> 00:28:13,559
Grandpa, are you okay?

589
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:15,359
Don't scare me.

590
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:18,759
Are you okay?

591
00:28:21,960 --> 00:28:22,799
Grandpa!

592
00:28:30,680 --> 00:28:31,839
Hello, Sister Ding Ning.

593
00:28:31,839 --> 00:28:32,640
Come quickly!

594
00:28:32,759 --> 00:28:33,799
Grandpa fainted!

595
00:28:35,319 --> 00:28:37,240
It's just a bit of low blood sugar.

596
00:28:37,839 --> 00:28:39,559
Have something to eat and you'll be fine.

597
00:28:39,640 --> 00:28:40,400
Got it.

598
00:28:41,279 --> 00:28:42,880
You scared Awu to death.

599
00:28:43,079 --> 00:28:45,000
Good thing he called me to come back.

600
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:48,519
It seems that new car Zhao Yijie gave you

601
00:28:48,519 --> 00:28:50,119
...actually did some good.

602
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:53,240
Otherwise, how could you have rushed back

603
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:54,279
...to save me?

604
00:28:57,559 --> 00:28:59,400
I went to see Mrs. Liang a few days ago.

605
00:29:02,640 --> 00:29:04,079
I know where the Sham Litigation Base...

606
00:29:04,079 --> 00:29:04,880
...is located.

607
00:29:06,279 --> 00:29:08,920
Should I ask Ma Tingting out to meet you?

608
00:29:10,160 --> 00:29:11,039
Not right now.

609
00:29:11,440 --> 00:29:12,400
Let me think about it.

610
00:29:15,279 --> 00:29:16,039
By the way.

611
00:29:17,160 --> 00:29:18,799
Have you been hearing cicadas recently?

612
00:29:24,799 --> 00:29:25,920
I'm a bit curious.

613
00:29:26,599 --> 00:29:28,519
Why do you always hear cicadas...

614
00:29:28,519 --> 00:29:30,559
...instead of birds singing...

615
00:29:30,559 --> 00:29:32,559
...or some other sounds?

616
00:29:32,559 --> 00:29:35,119
I find it strange, too.

617
00:29:36,200 --> 00:29:38,640
Maybe it's because my son, Xiao Yue...

618
00:29:39,039 --> 00:29:42,480
...used to talk to me about cicadas a lot.

619
00:29:43,319 --> 00:29:44,880
Actually, cicadas are amazing.

620
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:48,119
They can lie dormant for twelve years.

621
00:29:48,119 --> 00:29:51,000
Then emerge to molt in the thirteenth.

622
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:53,000
Only to live for one summer before dying.

623
00:29:56,559 --> 00:29:58,559
Twelve years for a single summer.

624
00:29:59,839 --> 00:30:01,480
I wonder if it's a bad deal.

625
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:04,559
Can you make a decision tomorrow?

626
00:30:19,960 --> 00:30:20,640
Looking for me?

627
00:30:23,759 --> 00:30:24,559
I called you,

628
00:30:24,559 --> 00:30:26,000
but you didn't answer, as usual.

629
00:30:26,279 --> 00:30:27,279
So I came over here.

630
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:29,000
So, as usual, you

631
00:30:29,200 --> 00:30:30,720
came straight to my door to confront me.

632
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:38,319
The last time we met

633
00:30:38,319 --> 00:30:39,960
was about the nursing home case, right?

634
00:30:41,160 --> 00:30:43,079
Yeah, it's a small world.

635
00:30:45,039 --> 00:30:46,880
Go ahead. What is it?

636
00:30:50,920 --> 00:30:52,039
I read the indictment.

637
00:30:52,920 --> 00:30:54,279
On Liang Zidong's case,

638
00:30:54,440 --> 00:30:56,359
you signed for the Prosecutor's Office.

639
00:30:56,799 --> 00:30:57,720
But I'm guessing

640
00:30:58,119 --> 00:30:59,240
you have other colleagues

641
00:30:59,240 --> 00:31:01,000
looking into the Fuxia Group, right?

642
00:31:06,279 --> 00:31:08,119
I know where the Sham Litigation Base is.

643
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:13,319
But I don't advise making a move now.

644
00:31:13,319 --> 00:31:14,119
Lawyer Ding,

645
00:31:14,839 --> 00:31:16,240
regardless of how many differences

646
00:31:16,240 --> 00:31:17,319
we've had in handling past cases,

647
00:31:17,440 --> 00:31:18,519
I believe

648
00:31:18,599 --> 00:31:20,480
our attitude toward crime

649
00:31:20,480 --> 00:31:21,359
is exactly the same, right?

650
00:31:21,359 --> 00:31:22,079
Hold on.

651
00:31:23,480 --> 00:31:24,400
If you hear me out

652
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:25,559
and still insist on going,

653
00:31:25,799 --> 00:31:26,599
then I'll help you.

654
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:28,000
But let's be clear upfront,

655
00:31:28,319 --> 00:31:29,640
I won't be responsible for the fallout.

656
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:31,559
If you agree, I'll continue.

657
00:31:34,559 --> 00:31:35,519
Let me consult my superiors.

658
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:44,400
Ding Ning,

659
00:31:44,519 --> 00:31:45,519
you came to me

660
00:31:45,920 --> 00:31:47,039
saying you found

661
00:31:47,039 --> 00:31:49,240
the Sham Litigation Base tied to Fuxia Group.

662
00:31:49,839 --> 00:31:51,319
If this is true,

663
00:31:51,319 --> 00:31:52,359
it means

664
00:31:52,559 --> 00:31:55,400
you've helped us solve a major case.

665
00:31:55,400 --> 00:31:57,680
And for the clues you provided,

666
00:31:57,799 --> 00:31:59,559
we will commend and reward you.

667
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:01,119
I'm not here to take credit.

668
00:32:01,440 --> 00:32:02,920
I'm here to clear my name.

669
00:32:03,039 --> 00:32:03,960
I just found out

670
00:32:03,960 --> 00:32:06,319
there might be illegal activities,

671
00:32:06,400 --> 00:32:07,279
and I came to report them.

672
00:32:08,880 --> 00:32:09,880
Here to report again.

673
00:32:10,880 --> 00:32:12,119
But I'll repeat myself:

674
00:32:12,720 --> 00:32:14,799
I don't advise making a move now.

675
00:32:15,160 --> 00:32:15,960
What's your reason?

676
00:32:18,839 --> 00:32:20,559
Does none of you think

677
00:32:21,359 --> 00:32:23,319
that this whole thing is very fishy?

678
00:32:30,039 --> 00:32:31,319
Should my people step in?

679
00:32:31,759 --> 00:32:33,440
I think it's better if I go myself.

680
00:32:33,799 --> 00:32:34,599
What do you think?

681
00:32:59,799 --> 00:33:00,480
Mr. Bi,

682
00:33:02,279 --> 00:33:02,960
Go ahead.

683
00:33:04,839 --> 00:33:05,640
In 2019,

684
00:33:06,599 --> 00:33:08,680
when Jiangliu City sought investments,

685
00:33:08,880 --> 00:33:10,279
we set our sights on Fuxia Group.

686
00:33:10,720 --> 00:33:12,200
We wanted them to build a factory here.

687
00:33:12,599 --> 00:33:14,119
It wasn't just us back then. There were

688
00:33:14,240 --> 00:33:16,079
local governments from four other cities

689
00:33:16,079 --> 00:33:17,160
that all wanted them to move there.

690
00:33:18,160 --> 00:33:20,720
They offered all kinds of incentives.

691
00:33:21,039 --> 00:33:22,839
So we took an unconventional approach.

692
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:25,319
On the surface, it met national policies

693
00:33:25,519 --> 00:33:27,000
regarding their taxes,

694
00:33:27,039 --> 00:33:28,119
fines, and regulations.

695
00:33:29,359 --> 00:33:30,480
But in private, we...

696
00:33:30,759 --> 00:33:32,599
We used taxpayers' money

697
00:33:32,599 --> 00:33:34,200
to subsidize Fuxia Group.

698
00:33:34,400 --> 00:33:35,640
You and I did the math before.

699
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:37,640
As long as Fuxia was willing to come,

700
00:33:39,079 --> 00:33:40,640
for every ten yuan of public money spent,

701
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:42,200
we could get 32 yuan back.

702
00:33:42,599 --> 00:33:43,400
The price

703
00:33:44,319 --> 00:33:46,960
was that we all broke the laws and rules.

704
00:33:47,160 --> 00:33:48,759
But since 2019,

705
00:33:49,079 --> 00:33:50,720
Fuxia Group has been going downhill.

706
00:33:51,039 --> 00:33:53,400
Not only do they bring us no benefits,

707
00:33:53,400 --> 00:33:54,839
but because of environmental issues,

708
00:33:56,160 --> 00:33:58,400
they've become a burden we can't shake.

709
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:01,680
Mr. Bi,

710
00:34:03,240 --> 00:34:04,039
must a burden

711
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:07,000
be destroyed?

712
00:34:08,159 --> 00:34:09,639
The survival of Fuxia Group

713
00:34:09,639 --> 00:34:10,440
affects

714
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:12,880
the families and jobs of 10,000 employees.

715
00:34:16,800 --> 00:34:18,159
In our position,

716
00:34:18,360 --> 00:34:19,880
we must consider the long term.

717
00:34:20,480 --> 00:34:22,119
I know why you can't bring yourself to.

718
00:34:22,679 --> 00:34:24,159
Because once you do,

719
00:34:24,280 --> 00:34:25,239
it means

720
00:34:25,280 --> 00:34:26,679
all the hardships you've endured,

721
00:34:27,039 --> 00:34:28,320
the grievances you've suffered,

722
00:34:28,639 --> 00:34:30,039
and the risks you've taken

723
00:34:30,559 --> 00:34:31,599
will all be meaningless.

724
00:34:31,920 --> 00:34:32,639
However,

725
00:34:32,920 --> 00:34:33,960
Fuxia Group has now

726
00:34:34,239 --> 00:34:36,159
become an obstacle to our development.

727
00:34:37,079 --> 00:34:38,159
We must abandon it.

728
00:35:07,639 --> 00:35:08,880
Going to see Yu Songfan again.

729
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:12,039
I knew you weren't the type

730
00:35:12,039 --> 00:35:13,119
to be so stubborn.

731
00:35:13,119 --> 00:35:14,119
I'm glad you're back.

732
00:35:14,119 --> 00:35:15,280
Otherwise, with such a big operation,

733
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:16,639
someone needs to be in charge, right?

734
00:35:16,639 --> 00:35:17,559
Now I can go back to slacking off.

735
00:35:17,559 --> 00:35:18,280
Slacking off?

736
00:35:18,880 --> 00:35:19,679
Maybe another day.

737
00:35:21,679 --> 00:35:23,000
You still have to go tonight.

738
00:35:26,800 --> 00:35:27,440
How did it go?

739
00:35:27,440 --> 00:35:28,480
Is Ding Ning willing to go?

740
00:35:28,639 --> 00:35:29,559
Shouldn't be a problem.

741
00:35:30,199 --> 00:35:31,800
Did you need me for something?

742
00:35:34,679 --> 00:35:37,079
You must personally

743
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:39,199
place this in the Sham Litigation Base.

744
00:35:41,159 --> 00:35:41,840
Is this more material

745
00:35:41,840 --> 00:35:44,199
to frame some director or president?

746
00:35:46,239 --> 00:35:47,719
If you really want to join us,

747
00:35:48,079 --> 00:35:48,840
ask what you should ask,

748
00:35:48,840 --> 00:35:50,000
and don't ask what you shouldn't.

749
00:35:50,119 --> 00:35:51,800
When do you want me to put it in?

750
00:35:52,159 --> 00:35:53,480
I haven't decided yet, actually.

751
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:54,639
Tell you what,

752
00:35:54,679 --> 00:35:55,760
wait for my word.

753
00:35:56,440 --> 00:35:58,039
Once I find the right opportunity,

754
00:35:58,320 --> 00:35:59,320
I'll call to let you know.

755
00:35:59,320 --> 00:36:00,000
Okay.

756
00:36:02,760 --> 00:36:04,360
Also, take this.

757
00:36:06,199 --> 00:36:07,880
It's a gift from an elder.

758
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:09,719
This is for Yang Awu,

759
00:36:09,719 --> 00:36:11,840
a growth policy from an offshore bank.

760
00:36:12,039 --> 00:36:14,280
Once the kid turns eighteen,

761
00:36:14,480 --> 00:36:16,440
the bank will pay him 50,000 a year,

762
00:36:16,519 --> 00:36:19,639
until you two reunite in heaven.

763
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:24,760
Anything else?

764
00:36:27,719 --> 00:36:28,400
Thank you.

765
00:36:42,159 --> 00:36:45,000
Assistant Xiao Zhao, at your service.

766
00:36:47,920 --> 00:36:48,719
Where are you going?

767
00:36:50,639 --> 00:36:51,480
Let's chat.

768
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:55,599
Come here.

769
00:37:20,880 --> 00:37:21,679
Thank you.

770
00:37:22,320 --> 00:37:23,320
You're right.

771
00:37:24,360 --> 00:37:25,000
As for me,

772
00:37:27,239 --> 00:37:28,079
I blew the act.

773
00:37:29,159 --> 00:37:31,760
If you don't report the Sham Litigation Base,

774
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:34,159
or just drop Liang Zidong's case,

775
00:37:34,159 --> 00:37:35,519
I'll be the one to lose the most,

776
00:37:36,639 --> 00:37:37,400
not you.

777
00:37:38,760 --> 00:37:40,599
Actually, after meeting you and Lao Yu,

778
00:37:40,880 --> 00:37:41,960
I suddenly realized

779
00:37:41,960 --> 00:37:44,000
that I've been exhausted all along,

780
00:37:46,440 --> 00:37:48,360
but I didn't know how to rest.

781
00:37:50,559 --> 00:37:51,960
What exactly are you trying to say?

782
00:37:56,039 --> 00:37:59,800
I want to try something,

783
00:38:02,960 --> 00:38:05,000
which is opening up to someone.

784
00:38:06,159 --> 00:38:08,039
I want you to help me see

785
00:38:08,239 --> 00:38:09,320
if the first half of my life

786
00:38:09,320 --> 00:38:11,360
was meaningful at all,

787
00:38:13,280 --> 00:38:14,679
and if everything I've done

788
00:38:15,599 --> 00:38:17,159
is completely worthless.

789
00:38:23,800 --> 00:38:24,599
Ding Ning.

790
00:38:27,199 --> 00:38:28,599
What do you think of Chang Yu?

791
00:38:29,760 --> 00:38:31,000
You know Chang Yu?

792
00:38:32,639 --> 00:38:33,679
More than that.

793
00:38:36,039 --> 00:38:38,519
He was once one of the founders of Rujie.
